# Answering a question in your own words, and putting one away: ANSWERS=scripts/duo-markdown.json HEX=kept scripts/duo tap <ref> scripts/duo-ask-taps
# "Answer in your own words" on its card docks one box above the keyboard, replying to that
# question, with Send as note and Answer under it, dimmed until there are words; let go of empty,
# the page's message box comes back, as it does on its x.
# Words typed and not sent stay: the page closes, and the app starts again, and the card's row
# shows them, the keyboard down.
launch hexvoice:///?tasks=md
wait 3
tap ask-card
wait 1
shoot ask-rest
tap ask-own
wait 1
shoot ask-empty
tap Close, keeping your words
wait 1
no-keyboard after closing it
frame thread-write
shoot ask-empty-resting
tap ask-own
type ask-input Found one of them
above-keyboard ask-input
shoot ask-writing
tap back
wait 1
no-keyboard leaving the page
open hexvoice:///?tasks=md
wait 2
shoot ask-held
launch hexvoice:///?tasks=md
wait 3
no-keyboard opening on held words
shoot ask-held-relaunch
# A swipe left puts it away, as in Mail: its row folds to Not needed, with Undo.
swipe-left ask-card
wait 1
shoot ask-swiped
tap Not needed
wait 1
shoot ask-put-away
tap Undo
wait 1
shoot ask-back
# The same swipe on its row in the Tasks list.
launch hexvoice:///?tasks
wait 3
tap tasks-search
type tasks-search-field iPad
swipe-left markdown asks
wait 1
shoot row-swiped
tap Not needed
wait 1
shoot row-put-away
# A note says the question is still open; a long answer stays in sight as it grows; an answer
# folds the card to what was said and clears the words, so the next run starts on none.
launch hexvoice:///?tasks=md
wait 3
tap ask-own
type ask-input  and the other
tap Send as note
wait 1
no-keyboard after the note
frame thread-write
shoot ask-noted
tap ask-own
type ask-input Found both, and this answer runs on over three or four lines on the folded screen so the box has to grow
above-keyboard ask-input
shoot ask-long
tap ask-Answer
wait 1
shoot ask-answered
# Swiped away while typing, it lets go of the keyboard and the page's foot comes back. Only folded
# upright does the card stay in sight above the keyboard (on its side and open upright, the reply box
# and keyboard fill the window), so it's checked there. A note clears the words for the next run.
pose cover-up
launch hexvoice:///?tasks=md
wait 3
tap ask-own
type ask-input still
swipe-left ask-card
wait 1
tap Not needed
wait 1
no-keyboard after a swipe while typing
frame thread-write
tap Undo
wait 1
tap ask-own
tap Send as note
wait 1
